# {{ project_name }}

A CLI application built with [functualize](https://github.com/raicing-ai/functualize).

## Usage

Install the project in development mode:

```bash
pip install -e .
```

Run the default sample job:

```bash
{{ project_name }} sample run
```

Run with options:

```bash
{{ project_name }} sample run --target "universe" --dry-run
```

## Configuration

This project uses functualize's layered configuration system. Config files are
loaded in order of precedence (later overrides earlier):

1. `config.base.toml` — shared defaults for all environments
2. `config.dev.toml` — development overrides (higher log verbosity, local endpoints)
3. `config.prod.toml` — production overrides (lower verbosity, real endpoints)

Set the active environment via the `FUNCTUALIZE_ENV` environment variable:

```bash
export FUNCTUALIZE_ENV=dev   # loads config.base.toml + config.dev.toml
export FUNCTUALIZE_ENV=prod  # loads config.base.toml + config.prod.toml
```

Individual values can also be overridden by environment variables using the
`SECTION_KEY` naming convention (e.g. `SAMPLE_TARGET=world`).

## Extension Points

### Adding a new job

```bash
func scaffold add job my-new-job
```

This creates `src/{{ package_name }}/jobs/my_new_job.py` with a starter template
including a Pydantic config model and RunContext usage.

### Adding a plugin

```bash
func scaffold add plugin my-plugin
```

This creates `src/{{ package_name }}/plugins/my_plugin.py` implementing the
functualize plugin protocol (OutputRenderer or InputProvider).

### Adding a TUI screen

```bash
func scaffold add tui-screen my-screen
```

This creates a Textual Screen subclass and associated TCSS stylesheet in
`src/{{ package_name }}/screens/`.
